Advanced HVDC, multiterminal and AC/DC study (@pe-hvdc-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/High-Voltage-DC-Transmission-Singh.lingua#r_26QM8ZB3JZVW1D1TWRY8JXX3B4", #source "../sources/Advanced-Power-Electronics-Bhim-Singh.lingua#r_4249XQH4D831ATDY73HJHCPRAS", #source "../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3", #source "../sources/Brazilian-Distribution-and-Network-Requirements.lingua#r_447WGES28KC2NYSCXTRQSWN82Y", #electrical-power-engineering "../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3") { r_31ZWT05WVF9ATE10DVN2Q0B0HN
**Read:** [High Voltage DC Transmission — S. N. Singh](../sources/High-Voltage-DC-Transmission-Singh.lingua#r_26QM8ZB3JZVW1D1TWRY8JXX3B4), entire written course and substantial examples; [Advance Power Electronics — Bhim Singh, IIT Delhi](../sources/Advanced-Power-Electronics-Bhim-Singh.lingua#r_4249XQH4D831ATDY73HJHCPRAS), complete FACTS/HVDC/VSC modules; [DPsim — electromagnetic-transient and dynamic-phasor methods](../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3), whole applicable component/domain and solver methods; [Brazilian distribution and network requirements — ANEEL and ONS](../sources/Brazilian-Distribution-and-Network-Requirements.lingua#r_447WGES28KC2NYSCXTRQSWN82Y), complete actual applicable connection/operation procedures.

Complete all of [High Voltage DC Transmission — S. N. Singh](../sources/High-Voltage-DC-Transmission-Singh.lingua#r_26QM8ZB3JZVW1D1TWRY8JXX3B4) and the full relevant [Advance Power Electronics — Bhim Singh, IIT Delhi](../sources/Advanced-Power-Electronics-Bhim-Singh.lingua#r_4249XQH4D831ATDY73HJHCPRAS) HVDC/VSC development. Choose a documented two-terminal or bounded multiterminal link with explicit AC systems, converter type, line/cable, control, energy and protection models.

Derive steady AC/DC balances and control conditions, then compare a reduced dynamic model with an appropriate EMT representation for a commutation, current-limit or DC-fault question. Keep reference frames, voltage/power bases, device limits, filters and source strength consistent. A linearized AC DC-OPF calculation is not a model of the physical DC converter/link.

Compare an analytical limit, independent numerical formulation and a full published or suitable qualified physical case. Investigate loss of a terminal/AC reference, changed power command and restoration sequence with actual auxiliary and energy constraints. Explain the system and component observables and the domain in which the model supports them. The final study should connect converter physics and control with transmission service, insulation, protection and maintained operation, while exposing which construction/material details need additional specialist evidence.

**Continue:** [An integrated electrical-power-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
